codex
A stronger invariant removes the need for that lemma entirely: carry the initial value as an ordinary local variable and require at each loop head that `binAcc(current, accumulator)` equals the fixed `binCodes(original)`. One real iteration transforms that premise into the next loop-head premise by the supplied forward equation; at exit it directly yields the final digits. I’m adopting this executable invariant and deleting the attempted simplification rules.
