codex
That base lemma was too broad: making `binAcc` itself simplify under symbolic equality guards invites repeated case-splitting. I’m narrowing it to the actual Boolean obligation—rewrite only an equality of the form `binAcc(E, A) ==K B` when `E == 0`. This preserves the fixed base equation without changing symbolic evaluation of `binAcc` elsewhere.
