codex
A cleaner proof formulation avoids any connection lemma: make the postcondition relational. The loop may return an existential digit sequence, but it must satisfy the exact guarded base-2 recurrence from its starting integer and accumulator. The whole-function claim then requires the returned middle sequence to satisfy the decimal representation relation (`0 ↦ "0"`, positive values use that recurrence). This directly constrains the result without forcing recursive summaries to normalize ahead of execution.
